// spec: main is `int main()` or `int main(int argc, char** argv)`, C++'s two forms, which the program's entry calls (const anywhere in argv's pointers is fine); another form is an error: one parameter here, an environment parameter or a void result in the snippets beside it
// found by thread B (2026-11-06): the entry called main with no arguments when it took one, so this printed 0 in a release build (argc arrived by register luck at -O0)
// error: main is int main() or int main(int argc, char** argv)
extern "C" import "stdio.h";
int main(int argc)
{
  printf("%d\n", argc);
  return 0;
}
